            <div xml:id="d734">

                <pb facs="0793" n="689" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg689"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/5040: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Acting Secretary
                            of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-04-13T18:00:00+08:00">April 13, 1932—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 13—6:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>At a meeting today British Minister and I, Italian Chargé d’Affaires and
                    representative of French Minister, discussed necessity of retaining large forces
                    at Shanghai. British Minister informed me that he was informing his commander in
                    chief that he saw no objection from a political point of view to reducing
                    British forces here by one battalion. British Minister stated that he was making
                    this statement in reply to an inquiry from the admiral. I understood that
                    British forces will probably be reduced by this number shortly.</p>
                <p>I have informed Admiral Taylor of the
                    above.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
